      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_3",
        on: "start",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:scroll_to_unit",
            id: "Lady Jessene",
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:set_variable_dynamic",
            variable: "haldric_s.facing",
            value: "sw",
            mode: "value",
          },
          {
            tag: "set_variable",
            name: "haldric_s.x",
            value: 11,
          },
          {
            tag: "set_variable",
            name: "haldric_s.y",
            value: 7,
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:unstore_unit",
            variable: "haldric_s",
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:delay",
            time: 1250,
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Minister Edren",
            text: _("May Commander Aethyr have a peaceful journey into the next world, where he has been preceded by his wife and loving daughters. For his heroism in the face of adversity a place of glory is assured to him in the Halls of Light..."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            text: _("Without the Commander’s noble sacrifice we would have never carried the day. We have won a great victory here today but much has been lost. My father Eldaric and King Addroran have fallen, and with them many other good people. However, there is hope, and a new land is open before us!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            text: _("Jessene, you hid the ruby away in that vile troll hole? Didn’t you?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lady Jessene",
            text: _("What? Why would you doubt me?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            text: _("The orcs that didn’t escape in the ships have regrouped. They are preparing to march on the elves. We should come to the aid of our new friends."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            text: _("These orcs are few, but the elves aren’t accustomed to war. Besides we will have to rely on elven charity if we are to survive this first winter."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            text: _("After that, we should build towns in all of the regions that the elves have given us. We should move our capital inland, away from the coast. I hope the children of the good people of the west-north, of the Green Isle, find prosperity in this new land."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            text: _("I suppose I am King Haldric now. Hmm... but what to call this new kingdom?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lady Jessene",
            text: _("May I make a suggestion?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            text: _("Sure."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lady Jessene",
            text: _("The word ‘Wesfolk’ is from your old tongue. It means ‘People of the West’. The elves call us the people of the west-north. Under the same old tongue that would be ‘Wes Noth’. So I suggest that the new kingdom be called ‘Wesnoth’, in honor of our old home."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            text: _("Hmm. ‘Wesnoth’. I like it. Yes, ‘Wesnoth’ would be fine. So I am the first King of Wesnoth!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lady Jessene",
            text: _("So, what is to become of me?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            text: _("There are many Wesfolk amongst the remains of my people. We must stay united under one banner. I will need you by my side if there is any hope of building a true ‘Kingdom of Wesnoth’. I... I think a Queen’s crown would sit well upon that flame-colored hair of yours, Jessene."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lady Jessene",
            text: _("I am not to be bought with trinkets, Haldric."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Prince Haldric",
            text: _("Then take my hand, Jessene, if you won’t accept crown or kingdom. You have earned both. We can’t make this work without your people... and I don’t think I can make it work without <i>you</i>."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Lady Jessene",
            text: _("Probably not. And, if nothing else, the hero-king of Wesnoth, Haldric Dragonbane, will need someone to remind him that he does not eat lightning and belch thunder. I... accept."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: "wesnoth-icon.png",
            text: _("It was never said afterwards that the marriage of Haldric and Jessene was exactly tranquil. But it was also said that neither could long stand to be separated from the other, and she bore him strong children that mingled the blood of their diverse ancestries. Many followed their example, and the two refugee peoples from the Green Isle became fused into one in the new kingdom."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: "wesnoth-icon.png",
            text: _("In later ages the bards would sing ‘The Breaking of the Pact’, an epic tale of Haldric’s betrayal of the elves. They would whisper of the price he and his descendants would pay for that betrayal without knowing the whole truth."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: "wesnoth-icon.png",
            text: _("But some of us have remembered the true story of our arrival on this great continent. The true story of the Rise of Wesnoth."),
          },
          {
            tag: "win",
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
]
